From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 15:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] LifoAlloc: 16-byte alignment on PPC64 (fixes Ion crashes on
 big-endian)

FloatRegisters::SetType on PPC64 is __uint128_t (3 kinds x 32 registers do
not fit in 64 bits), so every LSafepoint / LiveRegisterSet has alignof 16.
These objects are placement-new'ed into TempAllocator / LifoAlloc memory,
which only guarantees LIFO_ALLOC_ALIGN = 8.

With -mcpu=powerpc64 (no VSX) GCC zero-initializes the 16-byte members with
AltiVec `stvx`, which silently ignores the low four bits of the effective
address. For an LSafepoint at an 8-mod-16 address the constructor therefore
zeroes 8 bytes *before* the object (clobbering whatever LifoAlloc handed out
just before it) and leaves the low 8 bytes of liveRegs_.fpus() holding
LifoAlloc's 0xce poison. Observed on big-endian POWER8 as
  Assertion failure: safepoint->liveRegs().empty(), RegisterAllocator.cpp
in a debug shell, and in release builds as random register-allocator
crashes (BacktrackingAllocator::mergeAndQueueRegisters) and Ion code loading
through r0 (`ld r8,0(0)`), i.e. Firefox dying within seconds unless
javascript.options.ion=false.

ppc64le builds use -mcpu=power8/power9 and get VSX stxvd2x, which tolerates
misalignment, so the same under-alignment is harmless there. Raising
LIFO_ALLOC_ALIGN to 16 on PPC64 gives the objects the alignment the compiler
is entitled to assume.
---
 js/src/ds/LifoAlloc.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/js/src/ds/LifoAlloc.h
+++ b/js/src/ds/LifoAlloc.h
@@ -387,7 +387,17 @@
   }
 };
 
+#if defined(__powerpc64__)
+// FloatRegisters::SetType is __uint128_t on PPC64, so LSafepoint and the
+// other LiveRegisterSet holders placed in TempAllocator memory require 16-byte
+// alignment. GCC relies on it: without VSX it zeroes such members with stvx,
+// which drops the low four address bits, so an 8-byte-aligned object is only
+// half initialized and the 8 bytes before it are clobbered. Provide the
+// alignment the compiler assumes.
+static const size_t LIFO_ALLOC_ALIGN = 16;
+#else
 static const size_t LIFO_ALLOC_ALIGN = 8;
+#endif
 
 MOZ_ALWAYS_INLINE
 uint8_t* AlignPtr(uint8_t* orig) {
